{"id": "EUVD-2026-48769", "enisaUuid": "9b892500-a37b-3b84-b3ba-3927a53e946d", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nio_uring/io-wq: re-check IO_WQ_BIT_EXIT for each linked work item\n\ncommit 10dc95939817 (\"io_uring/io-wq: check IO_WQ_BIT_EXIT inside work\nrun loop\") fixed the obvious case where io_worker_handle_work() took one\nexit-bit snapshot before draining pending work, but the fix stops one\nlevel too early.\n\nio_worker_handle_work() now re-checks IO_WQ_BIT_EXIT in its outer work\nrun loop, yet it still snapshots that bit once before processing a whole\ndependent linked-work chain. If io_wq_exit_start() sets IO_WQ_BIT_EXIT\nafter the first linked item has started, the remaining linked items can\nstill reuse stale do_kill = false, skip IO_WQ_WORK_CANCEL, and continue\nrunning after exit has begun.\n\nMove the check further inside, so it covers linked items too. Note: this\nis a syzbot special as it loves setting up tons of slow linked work on\nweird devices like msr that take forever to read, and immediately close\nthe ring. Exit then takes a long time.", "datePublished": "2026-07-25T08:51:03", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T01:23:50", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/14b7ecad2ec56699325180a744f4b19f046401bb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d179533c610e1b4c6aa436e3c1fd1b719d2c727c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6e2f51f3e06773c2ee98ad09738f0908b48f76f9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ea61b04e1d7242cb37f5ed2cc91cf21a493f6597", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b6f179a653a934736c88d820fe0098c3c2532549", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1636d85dc139b07c0449308f2bb5e0c7a2e0da99", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ab85765cbe3258b43dc6729af0e6ce3a87a133d8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/29bef9934b2521f787bb15dd1985d4c0d12ae02a"], "aliases": ["GHSA-rmw8-w7cg-rwfm", "CVE-2026-64425"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "02dd2bc0-04e9-3525-a7d4-eda414efbf49", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bdf0bf73006ea8af9327cdb85cfdff4c23a5f966 <1636d85dc139b07c0449308f2bb5e0c7a2e0da99"}, {"id": "091f4750-053c-39e5-977b-ae64a02f15e7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "10dc959398175736e495f71c771f8641e1ca1907 <ab85765cbe3258b43dc6729af0e6ce3a87a133d8"}, {"id": "1302f091-4c02-3c20-8421-cf96b3d7b73a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.10.253 <5.10.261"}, {"id": "1cc3b7cf-c5ae-3bee-9541-24ebe58afc35", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.261"}, {"id": "2de03cfd-4eb7-398d-aa76-b9360528c5de", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d05d99573f81a091547b1778b9a50120f5d6c68a <6e2f51f3e06773c2ee98ad09738f0908b48f76f9"}, {"id": "47c59bf3-c191-3eb9-ad30-1d5955b41312", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.1.167 <6.1.178"}, {"id": "47f2e82b-5e10-3d85-a00a-6e3ac4276e3e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.39"}, {"id": "53eb9ab2-8006-313c-aa09-85f6ab69d799", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "10dc959398175736e495f71c771f8641e1ca1907 <29bef9934b2521f787bb15dd1985d4c0d12ae02a"}, {"id": "56f07c2d-55e8-341c-afc9-5e1121f064c0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.212"}, {"id": "579307ba-662b-3953-9e1f-f02638bfdb47", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.18.8 <6.18.39"}, {"id": "786d49b4-4880-3988-82dc-2c2fc6bdcf2f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "27e47500fac23d15b7dc93ff650bc4844d2581bd <d179533c610e1b4c6aa436e3c1fd1b719d2c727c"}, {"id": "7b93b979-b0f9-38d1-8e17-c13e25227792", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "p